The ducks lay a total of (number of ducks x number of days per week x number of days per month x number of months per year).

The number of ducks is (number of ducks per day x number of days per week x number of weeks per month x number of months per year).

The number of days per week is (number of days per month x number of months per year).

The number of days per month is (number of months per year x number of months per year).

The number of months per year is (number of years per decade x number of years per decade).

The number of years per decade is (number of years per century x number of years per century).

The number of years per century is (number of years per millennium x number of years per millennium).

The number of years per millenni
